@startuml
title Adventure Files - Save or Update Character

actor "Authenticated User" as User

boundary "React Frontend" as Frontend

control "Express API" as API

participant "Supabase Auth" as Auth

database "PostgreSQL + RLS" as Database

== Character Creation ==

User -> Frontend: Complete stages 01 to 05

note right of Frontend
  01 - Identity
  02 - Origins
  03 - Equipment
  04 - Essence
  05 - Journey

  Preserve selections
  in the character draft.
end note

Frontend -> Frontend: Validate required selections

User -> Frontend: Open stage 06 - Final Review

Frontend --> User: Display complete character summary

note right of Frontend
  Name
  Class
  Ancestry
  Background
  Weapon
  Artifact
  Personality
  Aura
  Companion
  Motivation
end note

User -> Frontend: Click Save Character

== Frontend Validation ==

Frontend -> Frontend: Validate complete draft

alt Invalid character draft

    Frontend --> User: Show validation errors

    note right of Frontend
      Preserve entered values.

      Allow corrections without
      restarting the creator.
    end note

else Valid character draft

    Frontend -> Frontend: Prevent duplicate submissions

    == Authenticated API Request ==

    Frontend -> API: PUT /api/characters/me\nBearer access token\nComplete character payload

    API -> Auth: Validate access token

    Auth --> API: Verified user ID or authentication failure

    alt Invalid, expired, or missing token

        API --> Frontend: 401 Unauthorized

        Frontend --> User: Show authentication error

    else Verified user

        == Server Validation ==

        API -> API: Validate name and approved catalog slugs

        note right of API
          Validate all fields.

          Artifact is required.
          Companion supports none.
          Motivation is required.

          Reject unknown identifiers.
        end note

        API -> API: Derive user_id from verified identity

        alt Invalid character data

            API --> Frontend: 400 Validation error

            Frontend --> User: Show safe validation feedback

        else Valid character data

            == Database Persistence ==

            API -> Database: User-scoped update; insert if absent

            Database -> Database: Enforce RLS ownership\nand UNIQUE(user_id)

            note right of API
              On concurrent insert conflict
              (PostgreSQL 23505), retry
              the ownership-scoped update.
            end note

            alt Permission or persistence failure

                Database --> API: Database error

                API --> Frontend: Safe error response

                Frontend --> User: Show recoverable error

                note right of Frontend
                  Preserve the draft.

                  Do not report success
                  or create duplicates.
                end note

            else Character created or updated

                Database --> API: Own saved character record

                API --> Frontend: 201 Created or 200 OK

                Frontend -> Frontend: Update saved character state

                Frontend --> User: Display My Character

            end

        end

    end

end

== Security and Compatibility ==

note over API, Database
  Never trust client-provided user_id.

  Do not bypass RLS with
  privileged service-role access.

  Preserve the one-character-per-user rule.

  Validate approved catalog identifiers.

  Legacy records require compatibility
  handling before stricter constraints
  are introduced.

  Never silently overwrite existing
  character data during migration.
end note

@enduml